From: Claude (Anthropic AI) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvapi: Acknowledge NvAPI_D3D_SetReflexSync.

Streamline calls this once per frame when DLSS Frame Generation is on. With no
entry point registered it fails with NVAPI_NO_IMPLEMENTATION every time, and
measured on The Witcher 3 Remastered with DLSSGMode=2 and five generated frames
that was 200514 failed calls in 857 seconds — 234 per second, each one going
through nvapi_QueryInterface and taking the process wide registry mutex, from
the frame generator's Present thread.

The shim in sl.common.dll caches the resolved pointer, but a stored nullptr is
indistinguishable from "not resolved yet", so a missing entry point is re-looked
up on every call. Registering it makes the pointer non-null, the cache sticks
and the count drops to one.

This cannot make Reflex Sync work and that is permanent. The struct feeds the
NVIDIA user mode driver with display pacing data (vblankIntervalUs,
timeInQueueUs, timeInQueueUsTarget) and with driver side Dynamic Frame
Generation control (fgMultiplier, dfgMaxMultiplier, dfgTargetFps). Nothing in
this stack can receive any of it: ID3DLowLatencyDevice exposes sleep mode,
markers and latency queries only, VK_NV_low_latency2 has no notion of a vblank
interval or a frame multiplier, and VK_NV_present_metering carries
numFramesPerBatch, which belongs to NV_FLIP_CONFIG and NvAPI_D3D12_SetFlipConfig
rather than here. So the function validates its arguments, logs what was asked
for and returns NVAPI_OK without touching device state.

Returning OK rather than NO_IMPLEMENTATION is safe here, and that was checked
rather than assumed: in sl.dlss_g.dll the two wrappers that call this
(setDynamicMFGParams at 0x180064c40 and setReflexTiming at 0x180064ab0) are
invoked from five sites and every one of them discards the return value in al
without a test, and both function bodies return a constant on success. The two
status codes are behaviourally indistinguishable for that build. Registering the
entry point and then returning NO_IMPLEMENTATION would be the worst of the three
options: the shim would cache a valid pointer and keep making real cross DLL
calls, while the log storm stayed.

bEnable and bDisable are deliberately not routed into SetLatencySleepMode. That
call also carries lowLatencyBoost and minimumIntervalUs, which the application
owns through NvAPI_D3D_SetSleepMode, and re-issuing it from here would silently
overwrite both — the existing dedup in nvapi_d3d.cpp does not cover boost, so it
would not even be noticed. Upstream PR #396 does exactly that and was rejected.

Upstream rejected this shape of change (jp7677/dxvk-nvapi#396, 2026-09-21), so
this stays local. DXVK_NVAPI_DISABLE_ENTRYPOINTS=NvAPI_D3D_SetReflexSync
restores the previous behaviour without a rebuild.

Verified: compiles clean for x86_64 and i386 with the project's mingw toolchain,
zero warnings, and the resulting nvapi64.dll and nvapi.dll contain the log string
this function emits, which the previous build does not. NOT verified: the unit
tests from the design note were left out because they could not be compiled here
(they are behind -Denable_tests and x86_64 only), and the latency gain was never
measured in microseconds — only the removed operations were counted.

Author: Claude (Anthropic AI), commissioned and supervised by the repository owner.
diff --git a/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp b/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp
index 09fc384..0a5cd8f 100644
--- a/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp
+++ b/src/nvapi_d3d.cpp
@@ -378,3 +378,82 @@ NVAPI_FUNCTION NvAPI_D3D_SetLatencyMarker(IUnknown* pDev, NV_LATENCY_MARKER_PARA
             return Error(n, alreadyLoggedError);
     }
 }
+
+NVAPI_FUNCTION NvAPI_D3D_SetReflexSync(IUnknown* pDev, NV_SET_REFLEX_SYNC_PARAMS* pSetReflexSyncParams) {
+    static constexpr auto n = FUNC;
+    thread_local bool alreadyLoggedOk = false;
+    thread_local bool alreadyLoggedNoImplementation = false;
+
+    if (log::tracing())
+        log::trace(n, log::fmt::ptr(pDev), log::fmt::ptr(pSetReflexSyncParams));
+
+    // Reflex Sync feeds the NVIDIA UMD with display-pacing data (vblankIntervalUs,
+    // timeInQueueUs/timeInQueueUsTarget) and with driver-side Dynamic Frame
+    // Generation control (fgMultiplier, dfgMaxMultiplier, dfgTargetFps). None of
+    // that has a receiver here: ID3DLowLatencyDevice exposes sleep mode, markers
+    // and latency queries only, VK_NV_low_latency2 has no notion of a vblank
+    // interval or a frame multiplier, and VK_NV_present_metering carries
+    // numFramesPerBatch, which belongs to NV_FLIP_CONFIG/NvAPI_D3D12_SetFlipConfig
+    // and not here. So this entry point only acknowledges the request and records
+    // what was asked for; it deliberately changes no device state.
+    //
+    // In particular bEnable/bDisable are NOT routed into SetLatencySleepMode:
+    // that call also carries lowLatencyBoost and minimumIntervalUs, which the
+    // application owns through NvAPI_D3D_SetSleepMode, and re-issuing it from
+    // here would silently overwrite both.
+    static uint32_t lastFlags = UINT32_MAX;
+    static uint32_t lastVblankIntervalUs = UINT32_MAX;
+    static uint32_t lastTimeInQueueUsTarget = UINT32_MAX;
+    static uint32_t lastFgMultiplier = UINT32_MAX;
+    static uint32_t lastDfgMaxMultiplier = UINT32_MAX;
+    static uint32_t lastDfgTargetFps = UINT32_MAX;
+
+    if (!nvapiAdapterRegistry)
+        return ApiNotInitialized(n);
+
+    if (!pDev || !pSetReflexSyncParams)
+        return InvalidArgument(n);
+
+    if (pSetReflexSyncParams->version != NV_SET_REFLEX_SYNC_PARAMS_VER1)
+        return IncompatibleStructVersion(n, pSetReflexSyncParams->version);
+
+    if (env::needsUnsupportedLowLatencyDevice())
+        return NoImplementation(n, alreadyLoggedNoImplementation);
+
+    auto lowLatencyDevice = NvapiD3dLowLatencyDevice::GetOrCreate(pDev);
+    if (!lowLatencyDevice || !lowLatencyDevice->SupportsLowLatency())
+        return NoImplementation(n, alreadyLoggedNoImplementation);
+
+    // NvU8 fields have to be widened, otherwise the stream inserter writes them
+    // as characters. timeInQueueUs is intentionally not part of the comparison,
+    // it is a per-frame measurement and would log on every single call.
+    auto flags = static_cast<uint32_t>(pSetReflexSyncParams->bEnable)
+        | static_cast<uint32_t>(pSetReflexSyncParams->bDisable) << 1;
+    auto fgMultiplier = static_cast<uint32_t>(pSetReflexSyncParams->fgMultiplier);
+    auto dfgMaxMultiplier = static_cast<uint32_t>(pSetReflexSyncParams->dfgMaxMultiplier);
+
+    if (lastFlags != flags
+        || lastVblankIntervalUs != pSetReflexSyncParams->vblankIntervalUs
+        || lastTimeInQueueUsTarget != pSetReflexSyncParams->timeInQueueUsTarget
+        || lastFgMultiplier != fgMultiplier
+        || lastDfgMaxMultiplier != dfgMaxMultiplier
+        || lastDfgTargetFps != pSetReflexSyncParams->dfgTargetFps) {
+        lastFlags = flags;
+        lastVblankIntervalUs = pSetReflexSyncParams->vblankIntervalUs;
+        lastTimeInQueueUsTarget = pSetReflexSyncParams->timeInQueueUsTarget;
+        lastFgMultiplier = fgMultiplier;
+        lastDfgMaxMultiplier = dfgMaxMultiplier;
+        lastDfgTargetFps = pSetReflexSyncParams->dfgTargetFps;
+
+        return Ok(str::format(n,
+            " (", pSetReflexSyncParams->bDisable ? "Disable" : (pSetReflexSyncParams->bEnable ? "Enable" : "Update"),
+            ", acknowledged without applying:",
+            " vblankInterval=", pSetReflexSyncParams->vblankIntervalUs, "us",
+            ", timeInQueueTarget=", pSetReflexSyncParams->timeInQueueUsTarget, "us",
+            ", fgMultiplier=", fgMultiplier,
+            ", dfgMaxMultiplier=", dfgMaxMultiplier,
+            ", dfgTargetFps=", pSetReflexSyncParams->dfgTargetFps, ")"));
+    }
+
+    return Ok(n, alreadyLoggedOk);
+}
diff --git a/src/nvapi_interface.cpp b/src/nvapi_interface.cpp
index 3e45558..35a6549 100644
--- a/src/nvapi_interface.cpp
+++ b/src/nvapi_interface.cpp
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ NVAPI_QUERY_INTERFACE nvapi_QueryInterface(NvU32 id) {
     INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_D3D_Sleep)
     INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_D3D_GetLatency)
     INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_D3D_SetLatencyMarker)
+    INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_D3D_SetReflexSync)
     INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_Vulkan_InitLowLatencyDevice)
     INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_Vulkan_DestroyLowLatencyDevice)
     INSERT_AND_RETURN_WHEN_EQUALS(NvAPI_Vulkan_GetSleepStatus)
